OMNIBLOOM

CREDITS

Omnibloom exists because previous generations of developers chose to share their work with the world.

Rather than rebuilding everything from scratch, Omni stands upon decades of open-source software, research, engineering, and community effort. We are grateful to the individuals, teams, foundations, and organizations who allowed others to learn from, use, modify, and improve their work.

TO THE GIANTS BEFORE US

Thank you to those who published source code.

Thank you to those who opened their repositories.

Thank you to those who wrote documentation.

Thank you to those who fixed bugs nobody would ever notice.

Thank you to those who maintained projects for years with little recognition.

Thank you to those who chose to build in public so that future developers could learn from their work.

Omni is another link in that chain.

SPECIAL SHOUT-OUTS

uBlock Origin

Special thanks to Raymond Hill (gorhill) and all uBlock Origin contributors.

uBlock Origin set the standard for efficient, privacy-focused content filtering and demonstrated that powerful software does not need to be bloated or wasteful.

Thank you for helping create a better web.

FFmpeg

Special thanks to the FFmpeg team.

Your work has powered countless video platforms, streaming services, media applications, creative tools, and research projects around the world.

Thank you for building one of the most important multimedia projects ever created.

yt-dlp

Special thanks to the yt-dlp community.

Your project represents the best of open-source collaboration, persistence, and community-driven development.

Thank you to everyone who contributed code, testing, documentation, and support.

THE OPEN-SOURCE COMMUNITY

Special thanks to all developers and maintainers who shared their work through GitHub and other open development platforms.

Many of the ideas, techniques, fixes, optimizations, and lessons that helped create Omni were only possible because others chose to share their knowledge.

